# field-kit.allowlist — known-SAFE entity names (advisory silencer).
#
# Copy to  ~/.config/field-kit.allowlist  and add your own safe names.
# The entity-advisory scanner (bin/entity-advisory.py) already silences a large
# built-in tech vocabulary (GitHub, Python, Docker, your own OSS project names, …).
# Add here the safe proper nouns SPECIFIC TO YOU that would otherwise show up as
# "new" on every push — your name, collaborators, personal domains, public projects.
#
# This is the counterpart to the scrublist:
#   scrublist  = names to BLOCK (client/employer/host identifiers)
#   allowlist  = names that are SAFE (silence the advisory)
# Anything in NEITHER list gets flagged for you to triage.
#
# One term per line; blank lines and #-comments ignored. Safe to keep local; this
# .example ships only generic placeholders.

# ── You / your public identity ──────────────────────────────────────
<your-name>
<your-github-handle>
<your-personal-domain.com>

# ── Your public / open-source project names ─────────────────────────
<your-oss-project>

# ── Frequent collaborators / co-authors (public) ────────────────────
<collaborator-name>
